The [[Estádio do Dragão]] was selected by the UEFA Executive Committee during their meeting in [[Kyiv]] on 24 May 2018.<ref>{{cite web |date=8 May 2018 |title=UEFA Executive Committee agenda for Kyiv meeting |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0245-0f8e603ea9eb-32460bb75cf2-1000--uefa-executive-committee-agenda-for-kyiv-meeting/|website=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations}}</ref><ref name="venue"/>

===Relocation to Budapest===
As a result of the [[COVID-19 pandemic in Europe]], the previous season's club finals were postponed and relocated. This includes the [[2020 UEFA Champions League Final]], which the UEFA Executive Committee moved to the [[Estádio do Dragão]] in [[Porto]] on 17 June 2020. At the same time, UEFA postponed and relocated the Super Cup from the Estádio do Dragão to the [[Puskás Aréna]] in [[Budapest]].<ref name="ExCo 17 June"/>

==Pre-match==

===Ticketing===
Tickets were on sale for the general public until 9 September 2020.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0261-1053064aa854-a1592f832670-1000--super-cup-tickets-on-sale/ |title=Super Cup tickets on sale: apply before Wednesday deadline |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=7 September 2020}}</ref> Moreover, 3,000 tickets were available for the supporters of each team. In total, 15,500 tickets were sold.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0261-10735cb08dbd-62041a47bb3c-1000--safety-message-for-super-cup-fans/|title=UEFA Super Cup: fans must comply with special measures to protect health|publisher=[[UEFA]]|date=24 September 2020}}</ref> Strict hygiene measures, including social distancing and wearing of face masks when social distancing could not be respected, were in place during the match. Ticket holders from overseas had to present proof of a negative [[Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2|SARS-CoV-2]] [[COVID-19 testing|PCR test]] performed within three days of entry, and had to leave the country within 72 hours after their entry.

Despite [[Government of Hungary|Hungarian government]] insisting that the match would be safe to attend, there was opposition to the decision to have spectators. Hungarian politician Ildikó Borbély called the game an "unacceptable experiment", while [[List of Ministers-President of Bavaria|Minister President of Bavaria]] [[Markus Söder]] urged Bayern fans not to travel, fearing that the match could turn into a "hotbed for [[COVID-19]] to spread". Hungarian Medical Chamber advisor, [[Epidemiology|epidemiologist]] András Csilek, stated that the Chamber also considered it wrong, saying that it "carries unnecessary risk adding" and "shouldn't be allowed".<ref>{{Cite news |title=Fans at Super Cup in Hungary 'safe' |language=en-GB |work=BBC Sport |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/54270055|access-date=23 September 2020}}</ref>

===Officials===
On 15 September 2020, UEFA named English official [[Anthony Taylor (referee)|Anthony Taylor]] as the referee for the match. Taylor had been a [[FIFA International Referees List|FIFA referee]] since 2013, and previously worked as one of the [[Assistant referee (association football)#Additional assistant referee|additional assistant referees]] in the [[2014 UEFA Super Cup]], [[2015 UEFA Europa League Final]], [[2016 UEFA Champions League Final]] and [[UEFA Euro 2016 Final]]. He was joined by his fellow countrymen, with Gary Beswick and Adam Nunn as assistant referees, [[Stuart Attwell]] as the [[video assistant referee]] (VAR) and [[Paul Tierney (referee)|Paul Tierney]] as the assistant VAR. Israeli referee [[Orel Grinfeld]] served as the fourth official.<ref name="officials">{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0261-1060f62078f8-06953e10bb08-1000/ |title=Anthony Taylor to referee 2020 UEFA Super Cup |website=[[UEFA]] |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=15 September 2020 |access-date=15 September 2020}}</ref>

==Match==

===Summary===
Sevilla were awarded a penalty after 13 minutes when [[Ivan Rakitić]] was blocked and bundled over in the penalty area by [[David Alaba]]. [[Lucas Ocampos]] scored the penalty shooting to the left corner to put Sevilla ahead. [[Leon Goretzka]] made it 1–1 in the 34th minute, with a side foot finish to the left corner of the net after a take down assist from [[Robert Lewandowski]].<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/football/2020/sep/24/bayern-munich-sevilla-super-cup-match-report|title = Javi Martínez's extra-time header wins Super Cup for Bayern against Sevilla|date= 24 September 2020 |work=Guardian|access-date=25 September 2020}}</ref>	
The game went into [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]], with substitute [[Javi Martínez]] getting the winner for Bayern in the 104th minute with a powerful header to the top left corner of the net when the ball fell to him, after Sevilla goalkeeper [[Yassine Bounou]] had punched the ball back into play.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/54270055|title = Bayern Munich 2 Sevilla 1|date= 24 September 2020 |work=BBC Sport|access-date=25 September 2020}}</ref>

